    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1984-p9.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "We have \\[ \\begin{aligned} 4^{16}5^{25} &=2^{32}5^{25}\\\\ &=2^7\\cdot10^{25}\\\\ &=128\\cdot10^{25}. \\end{aligned} \\] This is \\(128\\) followed by \\(25\\) zeros, so it has \\(3+25=28\\) digits. Therefore, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Rewrite the power of \\(4\\) as a power of \\(2\\)",
        "Pair \\(25\\) factors of \\(2\\) with the \\(25\\) factors of \\(5\\)"
      ],
